cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use blockadapt, please cite it as below."
title: "blockadapt: online adaptation of vision-aided millimeter-wave blockage prediction from delayed received-power labels"
abstract: >-
  A vision-aided predictor of line-of-sight blockage on a millimeter-wave link loses accuracy at night and in
  other recording sessions. blockadapt compares, as online streams on DeepSense 6G scenarios 17-21, six
  label-free test-time adaptation methods (normalisation statistics, Tent, EATA, SAR, CoTTA, T3A) with
  adaptation from delayed self-labels that the link derives from its own received power one prediction horizon
  later: online fine-tuning and threshold re-calibration. It includes the power rule and its agreement with
  the dataset labels, a shuffled-batch control that separates stream correlation from the shift, and the
  tests that pin every reported number to the released result files.
type: software
